<td id="A2.T10.2.14.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;">75.22</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.14.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T10.2.14.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">81.83</span></td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.14.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.5pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T10.2.14.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">98.18</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Performance of Qwen-32B for different weight &amp; activation quantization settings.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Scale quantization analysis</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in the main text, microscaling formats adopt scale quantization to reduce memory storage overhead and accelerate dequantization operations. However, scale quantization may introduce additional error due to rounding of scales onto a coarser grid. Below we provide an analysis and explore alternative choices for scale quantization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">MXFP format adopts E8M0 grid with exponentially spaced levels. It allows to represent values with very small and large magnitude, yet the distance between adjacent levels can be pretty large resulting in large approximation errors. E4M3 grid used in NVFP, on the other hand, has much narrower dynamic range <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-448,448]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>448,448</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-448,448]</annotation></semantics></math> with levels spread more uniformly. We note, that the sign bit is in fact never utilized, given that the scale is a non-negative value by definition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Below, we explore several choices for 8-bit scale quantization with a fixed group size of 16. Specifically, we measure weight and activation <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}^{\mathrm{rel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}^{\mathrm{rel}}</annotation></semantics></math> for a range of EeMm formats with e + m = 7, as well as for E8M0 and INT8. For E8M0 scale quantization, we multiply the scale by 4/3 following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>, which yields an unbiased estimate of the original scale and reduces quantization error. Results for weight and activation quantization are shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix C Scale quantization analysis ‣ Bridging the Gap Between Promise and Performance for Microscaling FP4 Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A3.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix C Scale quantization analysis ‣ Bridging the Gap Between Promise and Performance for Microscaling FP4 Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.23202v1/rqe_weights_llama-3.1-8b-instruct-block_15.svg" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:521/261;" width="521" height="261"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span><math id="A3.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}^{\mathrm{rel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}^{\mathrm{rel}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the weights of 15th block in the Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct model.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.23202v1/rqe_activations_llama-3.1-8b-instruct-block15.svg" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:521/261;" width="521" height="261"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span><math id="A3.F8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}^{\mathrm{rel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}^{\mathrm{rel}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the activations of 15th block in the Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct model.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">One can observe that the E4M3 and E8M0 scales are not optimal for weight scale quantization. E4M3 and E8M0 increase <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}^{\mathrm{rel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}^{\mathrm{rel}}</annotation></semantics></math> by 10%, 40% on average, respectively.
At the same time, FP8 options with larger mantissa (E1M6-E3M4) as well as INT8 perform close to FP4 without scale quantization. The pattern for activation pattern is similar except for the case of <span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">down_proj</span> in feedforward layer, which is known to have a more heavy-tailed distribution with pronounced outliers. We note that the observed behavior generalizes to other models considered in our study.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Outliers Analysis</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma 1.</span>
Let <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{G}}H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>G</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{G}}H</annotation></semantics></math> be the normalized Hadamard matrix. <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal (<math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\top}U=I_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\top}U=I_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>). The error vectors are related by <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{x}=\widehat{x}-x=U^{\top}\widehat{y}-U^{\top}y=U^{\top}(\widehat{y}-y)=U^{\top}\varepsilon_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{x}=\widehat{x}-x=U^{\top}\widehat{y}-U^{\top}y=U^{\top}(\widehat{y}-y)=U^{\top}\varepsilon_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal, it preserves the Euclidean norm: <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{2}^{2}=\|U^{\top}\varepsilon_{y}\|_{2}^{2}=\|\varepsilon_{y}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{2}^{2}=\|U^{\top}\varepsilon_{y}\|_{2}^{2}=\|\varepsilon_{y}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The per-element Mean Squared Error (MSE) is defined as:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}(G)=\frac{1}{G}\,\mathbb{E}[\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{2}^{2}]=\frac{1}{G}\,\mathbb{E}[\|\varepsilon_{y}\|_{2}^{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>MSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}(G)=\frac{1}{G}\,\mathbb{E}[\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{2}^{2}]=\frac{1}{G}\,\mathbb{E}[\|\varepsilon_{y}\|_{2}^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This establishes the second equality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To prove the first, we rely on the standard assumption in quantization analysis that the quantization error <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is statistically independent of the signal <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> are related by the invertible transformation <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=U^{\top}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=U^{\top}y</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is also independent of <math id="A4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the reconstruction error <math id="A4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{x}=U^{\top}\varepsilon_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{x}=U^{\top}\varepsilon_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is also going to be independent of <math id="A4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The index <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\star}=\arg\max_{i}|x_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\star}=\arg\max_{i}|x_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the error vector <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> (and its components) is independent of the random index <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Further, since the coordinates of <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d., we can apply symmetry to obtain that the probability that any coordinate <math id="A4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has the largest magnitude is uniform: <math id="A4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(I_{\star}=i)=1/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(I_{\star}=i)=1/G</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We calculate the Top-Element MSE using the Law of Total Expectation:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>top</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}(G)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{I_{\star}}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{I_{\star}}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{G}\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{I_{\star}}^{2}\mid I_{\star}=i]P(I_{\star}=i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{G}\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{I_{\star}}^{2}\mid I_{\star}=i]P(I_{\star}=i)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{G}\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}\mid I_{\star}=i]\cdot\frac{1}{G}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{G}\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}\mid I_{\star}=i]\cdot\frac{1}{G}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of the event <math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{I_{\star}=i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{I_{\star}=i\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional expectation simplifies to <math id="A4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}\mid I_{\star}=i]=\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}\mid I_{\star}=i]=\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting yields:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>MSE</mi><mi>top</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}(G)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\mathbb{E}[(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{G}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{G}(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}\right]\quad(\text{by linearity of expectation})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>by linearity of expectation</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{G}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{G}(\varepsilon_{x})_{i}^{2}\right]\quad(\text{by linearity of expectation})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{G}\mathbb{E}[\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{2}^{2}]=\mathrm{MSE}(G)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>MSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{G}\mathbb{E}[\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{2}^{2}]=\mathrm{MSE}(G).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.3" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Outliers MAPE)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let distribution <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> be a mix of two distributions: <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{base}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{base}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{outliers}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{outliers}</annotation></semantics></math> with portions <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(|\mathcal{X}_{outliers}|)&gt;\max(|\mathcal{X}_{base}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(|\mathcal{X}_{outliers}|)&gt;\max(|\mathcal{X}_{base}|)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(X\sim\mathcal{X}|X_{I_{\star}}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers})=\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(X\sim\mathcal{X}|X_{I_{\star}}\sim\mathcal{X}_{base})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>top</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>top</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(X\sim\mathcal{X}|X_{I_{\star}}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers})=\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(X\sim\mathcal{X}|X_{I_{\star}}\sim\mathcal{X}_{base})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\cdot G\ll\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(\mathcal{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>top</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\cdot G\ll\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(\mathcal{X})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then the expected outlier relative quadratic error equals <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(\mathcal{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>top</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(\mathcal{X})</annotation></semantics></math> up to <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(pG)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(pG)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{X}}\!\left[\frac{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{G}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}\cdot\frac{(X_{i}-\widehat{X}_{i})^{2}}{X_{i}^{2}}}{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{G}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}}\right]\approx\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(X\sim\mathcal{X})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>top</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{X}}\!\left[\frac{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{G}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}\cdot\frac{(X_{i}-\widehat{X}_{i})^{2}}{X_{i}^{2}}}{\sum\limits_{i=1}^{G}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}}\right]\approx\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(X\sim\mathcal{X}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We expand the expectation conditioned on <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{I_{\star}}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{I_{\star}}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{X}}\left[\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{G}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}\cdot\frac{(X_{i}-\widehat{X}_{i})^{2}}{X_{i}^{2}}}{\sum_{i=1}^{G}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{X}}\left[\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{G}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}\cdot\frac{(X_{i}-\widehat{X}_{i})^{2}}{X_{i}^{2}}}{\sum_{i=1}^{G}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{X}\,|\,X_{I_{\star}}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}\!\left[\frac{\frac{(X_{I_{\star}}-\widehat{X}_{I_{\star}})^{2}}{X_{I_{\star}}^{2}}+\sum_{i\neq I_{\star}}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}\cdot\frac{(X_{i}-\widehat{X}_{i})^{2}}{X_{i}^{2}}}{1+\sum_{i\neq I_{\star}}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.448em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{X}\,|\,X_{I_{\star}}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}\!\left[\frac{\frac{(X_{I_{\star}}-\widehat{X}_{I_{\star}})^{2}}{X_{I_{\star}}^{2}}+\sum_{i\neq I_{\star}}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}\cdot\frac{(X_{i}-\widehat{X}_{i})^{2}}{X_{i}^{2}}}{1+\sum_{i\neq I_{\star}}\lambda_{X_{i}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{X}\,|\,X_{I_{\star}}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}\!\left[\frac{(X_{I_{\star}}-\widehat{X}_{I_{\star}})^{2}}{X_{I_{\star}}^{2}}\right]+O(pG)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.448em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{X}\,|\,X_{I_{\star}}\sim\mathcal{X}_{outliers}}\!\left[\frac{(X_{I_{\star}}-\widehat{X}_{I_{\star}})^{2}}{X_{I_{\star}}^{2}}\right]+O(pG).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption 2 this conditional expectation equals <math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(\mathcal{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>top</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}(\mathcal{X})</annotation></semantics></math>, up to <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(pG)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(pG)</annotation></semantics></math> from Assumption 3. Hence the claim follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption 1 is satisfied for outliers chosen by absolute value thresholds.
Assumption 2 holds for floating-point quantization due to constant relative accuracy (no overflow/underflow), verified in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Numerical Validation ‣ 3 A Quantization Error Analysis of NVFP4 and MXFP4 ‣ Bridging the Gap Between Promise and Performance for Microscaling FP4 Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.
Assumption 3 holds in practice for LLMs since outliers are typically about <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1\%</annotation></semantics></math> of elements <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Consistency of <math id="Thmlemma4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>top</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{top}}^{\mathrm{rel}}</annotation></semantics></math> for smooth distributions)<span id="Thmlemma4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> be a distribution of values to quantize with a power-of-two translation-invariant quantization function</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q:\forall x\in\mathbb{R}_{+},\forall k\in\mathbb{Z}:Q(x\cdot 2^{k})=2^{k}\cdot Q(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q:\forall x\in\mathbb{R}_{+},\forall k\in\mathbb{Z}:Q(x\cdot 2^{k})=2^{k}\cdot Q(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume:</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\supp\mathcal{X}\subset[2^{a},2^{b}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\supp\mathcal{X}\subset[2^{a},2^{b}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for integers </span><math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&lt;b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall x\in\supp\mathcal{X},\forall y\in[x/\sqrt{2},x\cdot\sqrt{2}]:|f_{\mathcal{X}}(x)-f_{\mathcal{X}}(y)|\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall x\in\supp\mathcal{X},\forall y\in[x/\sqrt{2},x\cdot\sqrt{2}]:|f_{\mathcal{X}}(x)-f_{\mathcal{X}}(y)|\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}\leq\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{max}}^{\mathrm{rel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>max</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}\leq\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{max}}^{\mathrm{rel}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}\!\left[\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}\right]=\int_{1}^{2}\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}\,dx\;+\;O\!\left((2^{b}-2^{a})\,\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{max}}^{\mathrm{rel}}\cdot\alpha\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>max</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}\!\left[\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}\right]=\int_{1}^{2}\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}\,dx\;+\;O\!\left((2^{b}-2^{a})\,\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{max}}^{\mathrm{rel}}\cdot\alpha\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We decompose the expectation over dyadic intervals:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}\!\left[\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{X}}\!\left[\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=a}^{b-1}\int_{2^{i}}^{2^{i+1}}\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}f_{\mathcal{X}}(x)\,dx." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msup><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=a}^{b-1}\int_{2^{i}}^{2^{i+1}}\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}f_{\mathcal{X}}(x)\,dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Within each interval, write <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{X}}(x)=f_{\mathcal{X}}(2^{i})+(f_{\mathcal{X}}(x)-f_{\mathcal{X}}(2^{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{X}}(x)=f_{\mathcal{X}}(2^{i})+(f_{\mathcal{X}}(x)-f_{\mathcal{X}}(2^{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
The first term yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{1}^{2}\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}\,dx\cdot\sum_{i=a}^{b-1}2^{i}f_{\mathcal{X}}(2^{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{1}^{2}\frac{(x-Q(x))^{2}}{x^{2}}\,dx\cdot\sum_{i=a}^{b-1}2^{i}f_{\mathcal{X}}(2^{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The second term is bounded using Assumption 2 and 3, giving</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=a}^{b-1}\int_{2^{i}}^{2^{i+1}}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{max}}^{\mathrm{rel}}\cdot O(\alpha)\,dx=(2^{b}-2^{a})\cdot\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{max}}^{\mathrm{rel}}\cdot O(\alpha)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msup><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msubsup><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>max</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>MSE</mi><mi>max</mi><mi>rel</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=a}^{b-1}\int_{2^{i}}^{2^{i+1}}\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{max}}^{\mathrm{rel}}\cdot O(\alpha)\,dx=(2^{b}-2^{a})\cdot\mathrm{MSE}_{\mathrm{max}}^{\mathrm{rel}}\cdot O(\alpha).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, the normalization error in the discrete approximation of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int f_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int f_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> contributes an additional <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> factor. Combining terms gives the stated result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assumptions 1 and 3 hold for <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">absmax</span> <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{I_{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{I_{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> quantization since floating-point values are bounded with bounded relative error.
Assumption 2 is supported empirically (Figure <a href="#S3.F3.fig1" title="Figure 3 ‣ Shared Scales Quantization. ‣ 3.2 Numerical Validation ‣ 3 A Quantization Error Analysis of NVFP4 and MXFP4 ‣ Bridging the Gap Between Promise and Performance for Microscaling FP4 Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), where scale distributions are observed to be smooth.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>QuTLASS results on GeForce GPUs</h2>

<figure id="A5.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A5.F9.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.23202v1/flops_mxfp4_sm120.svg" id="A5.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/412;" width="548" height="412"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A5.F9.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.23202v1/figures/qwen3-8b-end-to-end-prefill-speedup-mxfp4-vs-bf16-on-rtx5090.png" id="A5.F9.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/340;" width="548" height="340" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Illustration of QuTLASS performance for weights and activations on MXFP4 while increasing batch size, for a single linear LLM layer, showing the low-overhead of the quantization-related ops, and end-to-end using the Transformers library.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Appendix E QuTLASS results on GeForce GPUs ‣ Bridging the Gap Between Promise and Performance for Microscaling FP4 Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> illustrates additional QuTLASS performance results on an NVIDIA RTX5090 GPU.
The figure on the left shows throughput for a single layer extracted from a MXPF4 quantized Qwen3-32B model, while the figure on the right shows the end-to-end speedups on Transformers running Qwen3-8B with MXFP4 quantization compared to the BF16 baseline implementation on a single RTX5090 GPU.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Standard deviation</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We estimate the variance of evaluation scores by performing multiple quantization runs on Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, varying the seeds for GPTQ calibration set sampling, as well as the strategies for scale selection and quantization ordering. These results were generated using our vLLM integration with QuTLASS kernels. Figure <a href="#A6.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix F Standard deviation ‣ Bridging the Gap Between Promise and Performance for Microscaling FP4 Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> displays the scores as bar plots, while Table <a href="#A6.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix F Standard deviation ‣ Bridging the Gap Between Promise and Performance for Microscaling FP4 Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> lists the average recovery scores and their standard deviations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, we report the average recovery scores and their standard deviations for the Platinum benchmark suite <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite> in Figure <a href="#A6.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ Appendix F Standard deviation ‣ Bridging the Gap Between Promise and Performance for Microscaling FP4 Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> and Table <a href="#A6.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix F Standard deviation ‣ Bridging the Gap Between Promise and Performance for Microscaling FP4 Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. We also report per-task recovery (</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A6.F10.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.23202v1/nvfp_std_boxplots_by_method.svg" id="A6.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/244;" width="548" height="244"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A6.F10.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.23202v1/mxfp_std_boxplots_by_method.svg" id="A6.F10.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/244;" width="548" height="244"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>Accuracy results for NVFP4 and MXFP4 across different combinations of MR-GPTQ components, averaged over five random seeds using vLLM kernels on the benchmark suite.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Accuracy results for MXFP4 across different MR-GPTQ component combinations on the Platinum benchmark tasks.</figcaption><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.23202v1/MXFP_benchmark_recoveries_platinum_bench_greens.svg" id="A6.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/305;" width="548" height="305"></object>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F12" class="ltx_figure">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Accuracy results for NVFP4 across different MR-GPTQ component combinations on the Platinum benchmark tasks.</figcaption><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.23202v1/NVFP_benchmark_recoveries_platinum_bench_greens.svg" id="A6.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/305;" width="548" height="305"></object>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A6.F13.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.23202v1/NVFP_std_boxplots_by_method_platinum.svg" id="A6.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/244;" width="548" height="244"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A6.F13.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.23202v1/MXFP_std_boxplots_by_method_platinum.svg" id="A6.F13.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/244;" width="548" height="244"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span>Average recovery scores and standard deviations for NVFP and MXFP methods on the Platinum benchmarks.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.T11" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A6.T11.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A6.T11.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
